From 2c742991466c06129a014171faaa7b7a9f121e3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Frdlik <michaelf.ms@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 09:51:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] Thylacine Warp V-3b-3c-2b: the vn_renderer
 device-memory bo_ops + the vkAllocateMemory E2E

Fill the three pre-wired device-memory bo_ops over the 3c-2a mem/ ABI, so a
HOST_VISIBLE vkAllocateMemory + vkMapMemory round-trips end-to-end on real V3D
(thyla-pi/KVM, Virtio-GPU Venus V3D 4.2.14): device-memory sentinel OK
(zero-at-map + c0deface round-tripped) -> THYLACINE-VENUS-PROVE PASS.

- thylacine_bo_create_from_device_memory: page-round + guard <= 64 MiB, alloc a
  client handle from a 256-slot mem_bitmap, warp_mem_new "<bytes> <handle>
  <mem_id>" (blob_id = the Venus memory object id), store the bo in bo_array
  keyed by res_id.
- thylacine_bo_map: lazy warp_mem_map -> t_weft_map (the client holds no PCI
  handle, so weft not SYS_BURROW_FROM_HOSTMEM), cached.
- thylacine_bo_destroy: unmap -> warp_mem_destroy -> free the handle ONLY on a
  confirmed server retire (the two-sided guest-handle-free <=> server-slot-free
  invariant, mirroring the ring ridx).
- Transport warp_mem_{new,map,unmap,destroy} mirror the ring verbs.

Two masking-bug layers under the first vkCreateDevice ever run on real V3D
(V-3b-3b stopped at instance):
- The loader trampoline: vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr returns mesa LOADER dispatch
  trampolines built for the loader's object layout; loader-less the
  physical-device CreateDevice slot is null -> tail-branch to pc=0. Fix: call the
  Venus entrypoints directly by symbol (extern vn_CreateDevice / vn_AllocateMemory
  / the 1.4 vn_MapMemory2 / vn_UnmapMemory2 / vn_FreeMemory / vn_DestroyDevice),
  the loader-less pattern the prove already used for the ICD entry.
- The timeline cap: vn_instance_acquire_ring_idx reserves ring 0 for the CPU
  timeline and hands a queue index 1, rejected when >= max_timeline_count; the
  V-3b-3b F3 cap of 1 made EVERY vkCreateDevice-with-a-queue impossible. Fix:
  max_timeline_count = 2 (exactly one queue timeline, self-limiting).

Audit (holotype-reviewer Fable 5 max, I-45 client surface): 0 P0 / 2 P1 / 0 P2
/ 1 P3, all fixed -- DIRTY close, re-audit owed on the fixes.
- F1 [P1]: the F4 mint-before-device-use ordering was NOT honored -- the driving
  Venus flow defers renderer-bo creation to first vkMapMemory for a plain
  HOST_VISIBLE type, so the server's mint-time zeroing would destroy a GPU write
  landed between allocate and first map. Fix: a new vn_renderer_info bit
  bo_must_init_at_alloc; vn_device_memory reifies the bo (and so the mint) at
  vkAllocateMemory for HOST_VISIBLE when set (alloc_export's eager tail). The
  black-box E2E cannot witness the ordering (needs a GPU write, i.e. a submit) --
  the regression witness lands with the GPU-submit chunk.
- F2 [P1]: every refused mint permanently burned a handle, and for mem the
  dominant refusal is the routine E_NOMEM at the 64 MiB holistic cap -> <=256
  refusals wedged vkAllocateMemory for the instance's life. Fix: warp_mem_new is
  three-valued (1 = server slot provably NOT installed -> free the handle; -1 =
  maybe installed -> keep marked); the backend frees on the not-installed arm.
- F3 [P3]: the timeline comment overclaimed single-queue submit-fence soundness
  (creation is sound; submit fencing is part of the owed F3 work) -> reworded.

Gate-wired (#245): the client witness "device-memory sentinel OK" joins the
venus gate + test-venus-verdict (DISCRIMINATES 37/37) + the boot-probe filter.
The core Venus driver stays otherwise pristine (localization probes reverted;
the only vn_device_memory / vn_renderer.h change is the F1 reify-at-alloc bit).

OWED: the F1/F2 regression witnesses (both need a GPU submit / cap-exhaustion
harness); the F2 rc<0 convergence; the F3 seam-carries-ring_idx + submit-fence
analysis; the multi-thread warp_conn/bitmap mutex; the dirty-close re-audit.

